1
00:00:00,330 --> 00:00:02,270
This bee is giving directions.

2
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:04,795
Her dance tells the colony
where the food is.

3
00:00:05,412 --> 00:00:07,012
Inside the hive it's dark,

4
00:00:07,012 --> 00:00:09,012
and the comb is a vertical wall.

5
00:00:09,162 --> 00:00:11,422
She can't point
at the flowers from in here.

6
00:00:11,422 --> 00:00:12,627
So she dances.

7
00:00:13,254 --> 00:00:14,194
On the comb,

8
00:00:14,194 --> 00:00:15,924
straight up means toward the sun.

9
00:00:16,166 --> 00:00:18,604
Food forty-five degrees right of the sun?

10
00:00:18,604 --> 00:00:21,954
Her waggle run leans forty-five
degrees right of straight up.

11
00:00:22,233 --> 00:00:23,449
As the sun moves,

12
00:00:23,449 --> 00:00:25,307
she shifts her angle to match.

13
00:00:25,934 --> 00:00:29,841
She repeats the loop, turning left,
then right: a figure-eight.

14
00:00:29,841 --> 00:00:32,094
The waggle run carries the distance.

15
00:00:32,145 --> 00:00:33,264
The farther the food,

16
00:00:33,264 --> 00:00:34,691
the longer she waggles.

17
00:00:35,338 --> 00:00:37,918
For very close food, about ten metres,

18
00:00:37,918 --> 00:00:40,258
she runs in a small circle instead.

19
00:00:40,448 --> 00:00:42,058
Past about forty metres,

20
00:00:42,058 --> 00:00:44,423
the circle stretches
into the waggle dance.

21
00:00:45,030 --> 00:00:46,536
Karl von Frisch,

22
00:00:46,536 --> 00:00:51,040
the Austrian scientist who
shared the 1973 Nobel Prize,

23
00:00:51,090 --> 00:00:52,930
was one of the first to decode it.
